+### Topology-controlled Transfer Function UI
+The Topology-controlled Transfer Function UI allows users to select a topological zone in a rendered image by projecting a ray through the data from the pixel. The first 'visible' topological zone is selected by evaluating the volume rendering integral for the ray and finding the first sample with opacity above a threshold. The fully augmented contour tree is used to determine the topological zone to which the selected sample (from ray) or pixel (from slice) belongs. The contour tree is displayed in two representations: a TOPORRERY view (3D radial layout where height corresponds to function value) and a traditional 2D view (y-coordinate corresponds to function value). A vertical transfer function editor is included next to the contour tree interface, linking the y-coordinates of the contour tree interface and the transfer function editor to provide contextual topological information. For volume-rendered data with multiple layers, ray casting visibility is not straightforward; a slice view is provided as an alternative where the user selects the topological zone's intersection with that slice [S5].
 
